    <h2 class="h4">Keith's chapter</h2>
    <p>Keith Dunstan's contribution surveys Melbourne from its flat, tram-friendly geography and gold rush bravado through the crash of 1892 and its lasting inferiority complex, then takes the reader on a tour through Toorak, St Patrick's Cathedral, Parliament House and the Windsor Hotel, closing with restaurant recommendations ranging from Emil's in Lonsdale Street to Smacka Fitzgibbon's jazz bar in North Melbourne.</p>
